<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40417" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπαίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mock at</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.13
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				172.16
			</span></i>, with reference to the preceding line, where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπαίζεται</span> means <i>are an
			after-play</i>, in allusion to things eaten at a second course.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. <i>sport upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλάττῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.17
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
